<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela reiterates Placer, Cristinas.</title>
<headline>Venezuela reiterates Placer, Cristinas.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuelan Minister of Energy and Mines Erwin Arrieta reiterated Thursday Canadian mining company Placer Dome's rights to the Cristinas gold mine concession over rival claims by Crystallex.</p>
<p>&quot;There is no legal problem,&quot; Arrieta told reporters.</p>
<p>&quot;We are revising (doucments) to see the historical chain of possesion to the concession, but our legal advice has been that Placer is the concessionaire,&quot; Arrieta added.</p>
<p>Crystallex has laid claim to two blocks of the gold rich property in south-eastern Venezuela following a recent Venezuelan Supreme Court decision.</p>
</text>
